 "face": {
  "mode": "baked",
  "note": "The face is baked on the head: the eyes are glossy lenses (lo_eyes) with the blue iris, the pupil and two catchlights painted in; the closed smile, the brows and the closed lids' lash lines are baked into the body. No face sheet and no morphs: expressions in clips' `faces` are hints only; the mouth never opens. Blinking scales the blink bones (play `blink` over any clip): each lens squashes onto the painted lash line and sinks under the skin. The glow (ORM alpha, untinted, steady) is a soft fill on the underside (the studio light never reaches the white belly) and a faint light on the tusk's ridges and the fins' and the fluke's frost. socket_tusk is the tusk's point (the ice-lance effects), socket_tail the fluke (the snowflake trail).",
